REM Protects the narrowed conflicting-DECLARE and METHODRET checks: a program-level warning
REM for an unrelated resolved DECLARE pair, silence for a related pair and for an unresolvable
REM type, and a warning (never an error) for a method missing a value-returning METHODRET and
REM for a void method that returns a value.

class public FixtureShapeBase
classend

class public FixtureShapeChild extends FixtureShapeBase
classend

class public FixtureOtherShape
classend

DECLARE FixtureShapeBase shapeA!
DECLARE FixtureOtherShape shapeA!

DECLARE FixtureShapeBase shapeB!
DECLARE FixtureShapeChild shapeB!

DECLARE FixtureShapeBase shapeC!
DECLARE FixtureUndeclaredShape shapeC!

class public FixtureMethods
    method public BBjString getName()
    methodend

    method public void announce()
        methodret "hello"
    methodend

    method public BBjString getGreeting()
        methodret "hi"
    methodend
classend
